1
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,815
[nurse] Sir, you can go in now.

5
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,940
I wanted to talk to you face-to-face.

6
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:31,818
So I came to see you.

7
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:35,113
I went through all the tests.

8
00:02:36,073 --> 00:02:40,869
Had my blood drawn, gave a urine sample,
had things attached to my chest,

9
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:44,247
and even ran in place
until they told me to stop.

10
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:56,134
Your test results show
no abnormalities with your heart.

11
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:02,683
And your symptom is…

12
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:05,977
a racing heart?

13
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:09,606
Do you know when a soldier
is authorized to kill?

14
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:18,532
I'm a soldier, so I even get rewarded
for killing the enemy.

15
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:26,832
Anyway, lately my heart's
been pounding like it did

16
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:29,793
when I was about to make my first kill.

17
00:03:35,966 --> 00:03:40,470
There are many possible causes
of an abnormal heartbeat.

18
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:45,892
In your case,
I think it may be psychological.

19
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,980
But this is a surgical department.

20
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:56,236
How do you manage to sleep at night?

21
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:06,455
I don't have to answer questions
that aren't medically relevant, do I?

22
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:24,306
When I attack the enemy…

23
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:29,269
I strike fast and aggressively,
catching them off guard.

24
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,687
That's how I operate.

25
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,442
If I get the chance…

26
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,280
I won't hesitate for even a second.

27
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,120
[nurse] Sir, your consultation is over.

28
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:48,830
Please wait outside.

29
00:04:59,216 --> 00:05:00,592
Too much stress…

30
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:04,095
isn't good for your heart.

31
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:24,574
EPISODE 7
MONSTER

32
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:31,873
[Jieun] We've already talked about this.
It's over. We need to stop.

33
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:33,375
[Junghyeon] Come on, Jieun. Wait.

34
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,835
Let's go somewhere and talk.

35
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,711
You haven't been answering my calls.

36
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:38,421
[Jieun] You need to leave!

37
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,715
[Junghyeon] Jieun.

38
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,491
[Jisun] Junghyeon.

39
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,035
What are you doing here?

40
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,873
Oh, well…

41
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:17,878
The surgery schedule suddenly changed,
so I came to tell your sister.

42
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,257
You could've called her.

43
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:26,386
Yeah, but it's a really important surgery,

44
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,054
so I thought I'd tell her in person.

45
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:30,056
But I'm really busy,
so I should get going.

46
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,141
See you later.

47
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:48,283
[Jisun] Hyeongsu's out exercising
after dropping the kids off?

48
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:51,411
Yeah, he says he's gaining weight
around his waist. [chuckles]

49
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,164
-Want some coffee?
-Yeah.

50
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:58,001
What brings you here so early?

51
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:03,006
I put my house up for sale.
Priced it low for a quick sale.

52
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,635
I don't know what to feel.

53
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:07,844
[Jieun] Mmm.

54
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:09,596
I see.

55
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,642
I'm sure you'll find a good buyer.

56
00:07:13,725 --> 00:07:14,809
[Jisun] Yeah.

57
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:21,816
And I wanted to drop this off.

58
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:30,617
Oh, this.
I was wondering where I'd put it…

59
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,327
It was in Junghyeon's car.

60
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:37,332
Oh…

61
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:39,793
Junghyeon came looking for you.

62
00:07:40,669 --> 00:07:42,837
It was raining, so I lent it to him.

63
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:47,092
She must've left it in my car by accident.

64
00:07:47,175 --> 00:07:51,388
She was getting wet in the rain
the other day, so I gave her a ride.

65
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:57,644
-You lent it to him?
-[Jieun] Yeah.

66
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,813
Want milk in your coffee?

67
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,357
You don't take syrup, right?

68
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,821
If you lent it to him,
how come you didn't know where it was?

69
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,950
And it didn't rain that day.

70
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:18,790
Oh, it didn't?

71
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:25,213
[chuckles] Gosh, I've been
so scatterbrained with the kids lately.

72
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:28,049
I swear my brain's turning to mush.

73
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,801
That's why I need coffee.

74
00:08:30,427 --> 00:08:32,095
Do you want anything else?

75
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,972
Junghyeon told me a different story.

76
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:40,770
Huh? That's weird.

77
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:42,897
Even just now, I ran into Junghyeon.

78
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,486
Oh, well, maybe he was just passing by.

79
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,536
Why are you lying to me?

80
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,001
[Jieun] What are you talking about?

81
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,837
Junghyeon had that same look on his face.

82
00:09:06,588 --> 00:09:08,298
Like he wanted me to stop asking.

83
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,801
He was acting strange earlier too.

84
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:14,179
Why are you being so sensitive?

85
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,931
You always get hung up
on the smallest things--

86
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:20,393
Don't make it sound like
I'm the one acting weird!

87
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:25,273
I saw you talking to Junghyeon.

88
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:26,733
Don't lie to me, Jieun.

89
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:32,489
What's going on?

90
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:33,865
Why can't you tell me?

91
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,789
[Jieun] Because it's over now.

92
00:09:51,049 --> 00:09:52,592
You and Junghyeon…

93
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,532
You see, we…

94
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:21,121
We were both exhausted, Hyeongsu and I.

95
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:25,750
So whenever I saw
Junghyeon at the hospital,

96
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,628
it felt like I could finally relax.

97
00:10:29,504 --> 00:10:31,005
He always made me laugh, and…

98
00:10:32,924 --> 00:10:35,969
I don't even know why I did it.

99
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:46,938
You were the only person
in the world I could trust.

100
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:49,023
So how could you lie to me, Jieun?

101
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:51,818
It meant nothing.
It was just a mistake, Jisun.

102
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,823
[Hyeongsu] Honey, I'm home.

103
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:58,908
Man, it's hot.

104
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:01,828
Oh, Jisun, you're here too?

105
00:11:06,249 --> 00:11:07,417
Hey.

106
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:13,339
-Honey, did something happen?
-[door closes]

107
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,604
There's something I need to tell you.

108
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:41,367
[attorney] <i>Defamation,</i>
<i>spreading false information,</i>

109
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:44,913
<i>making false accusations</i>
<i>of sexual assault, trespassing…</i>

110
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:48,249
<i>Oh, and add threats and stalking.</i>

111
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,127
Nice. That's brutal.

112
00:11:52,462 --> 00:11:54,839
You've got the whole package there.

113
00:11:54,923 --> 00:11:55,924
But…

114
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:59,844
I'm thinking of making her pay in a way
that's more fitting than a lawsuit.

115
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,974
Yeah. Let's do that.

116
00:12:05,475 --> 00:12:06,476
All right.

117
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,813
Hello, sir. What brings you here?

118
00:12:10,897 --> 00:12:13,775
[director] What do you think of the design
for the Cardiovascular Center?

119
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,111
It looks great.

120
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:20,365
Guess who the director's going to be?

121
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:21,449
Who?

122
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:23,660
It's you, man.

123
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:25,411
What?

124
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:28,873
Thanks to you, our brand recognition
has jumped from eleventh to third place.

125
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,586
You better get us to number one
while you're running the center.

126
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:52,689
Jisun.

127
00:12:59,988 --> 00:13:02,740
Your sister told me what happened,
but you've got it all wrong.

128
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:09,747
Did you move to Sangcheon
because of my sister?

129
00:13:09,831 --> 00:13:11,124
-No.
-[Jisun] Was she the reason

130
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,875
you approached me in the first place?

131
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:15,169
Were you seeing her
while you were also dating me?

132
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:17,672
What are you talking about? Of course not.

133
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:20,717
You two must've had
a good laugh at my expense.

134
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,427
You've got it all wrong.

135
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:26,472
It's nothing like what you're imagining.

136
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,683
It was just…

137
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:31,352
It was just a brief thing.

138
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,187
People make mistakes, don't they?

139
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:35,940
Does one mistake
have to invalidate everything

140
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:37,692
-about me?
-Park Junghyeon.

141
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,736
Were you ever really my friend?

142
00:13:39,819 --> 00:13:42,280
Yes, I was. I still am.

143
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:43,656
I can't trust anyone anymore.

144
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,907
[Junghyeon] Jisun, wait…

145
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:51,080
Look, I'm sorry,
and I know how confused you must be,

146
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:55,585
but you're overreacting a little
by taking it this far.

147
00:13:59,422 --> 00:14:03,051
-Jisun, what I'm trying to say is--
-Don't make it sound like I'm the problem.

148
00:14:08,723 --> 00:14:09,724
[Junghyeon] Jisun.

149
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:30,912
MAY 5
INTERESTED

150
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,372
CAN WE MEET IN PERSON?

151
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,087
WEEKLY BESTSELLERS

152
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:40,963
GHB, DATE-RAPE DRUG, 50 ML

153
00:14:41,047 --> 00:14:42,757
PREMIUM ICE CRYSTALS, 1 G

154
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,967
NO IN-PERSON DEALS

155
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:53,893
PAYFUN OR CRYPTO ONLY

156
00:14:56,062 --> 00:15:00,358
I'M OLD-SCHOOL, I PREFER CASH
I'LL PAY 20% EXTRA

157
00:15:05,363 --> 00:15:06,405
200%

158
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:12,286
DEAL

159
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:13,746
[person] <i>Tomorrow at 8:00 p.m.</i>

160
00:15:14,372 --> 00:15:15,998
<i>Leave the payment by the fire hydrant</i>

161
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:18,209
<i>on the east side of Crown Village,</i>
<i>second floor.</i>

162
00:15:21,796 --> 00:15:23,548
-12 10-ML BOTTLES?
-ONLY 5-ML BOTTLES

163
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,842
-HOW MUCH LONGER?
-I'LL LET YOU KNOW

164
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,970
[person] <i>Once payment is confirmed,</i>
<i>pick up the goods today at 8:00 p.m.</i>

165
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:31,973
<i>by the fire hydrant on the west side</i>
<i>of Crown Village, third floor.</i>

166
00:17:57,368 --> 00:17:59,745
-[groans]
-Gosh, are you okay?

167
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:01,998
Goodness. You should've been careful.

168
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,292
Man… Are you all right?

169
00:18:04,375 --> 00:18:05,585
[Hwayoung] I'm sorry.

170
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:45,559
[Hwayoung] Damn it.

171
00:19:58,489 --> 00:20:00,241
I feel sickened by it all.

172
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,954
CLINIC DIRECTOR KIM JIAN

173
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:08,541
I feel confused and helpless…

174
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:16,590
I'm just so angry at him
that I can't stand it.

175
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:19,719
[Jian] What happened
between you and this man?

176
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:21,387
He sexually assaulted me.

177
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,056
[Jian] Oh, dear.

178
00:20:24,682 --> 00:20:26,225
Did you report it?

179
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:28,394
It didn't do any good.

180
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:33,023
They said there wasn't enough evidence,
so he wasn't punished at all.

181
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:44,410
Something similar happened to me before.

182
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,414
Back then, I tried to put it behind me
as quickly as possible

183
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:49,623
and pull myself together.

184
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:52,209
I tried everything I could think of.

185
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:56,964
Counseling, meditation, art therapy,
108 bows, pilgrimages to sacred sites…

186
00:21:00,176 --> 00:21:02,094
But none of it helped.

187
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,937
The people who committed these crimes
should be the ones suffering.

188
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:18,235
But instead,
I feel like I'm the one losing everything,

189
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:22,156
becoming some kind of troublemaker
who's not right in the head.

190
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:25,075
While those bastards
live their lives just fine.

191
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:32,166
Ms. Kang, let's try to stop
thinking about it for a minute--

192
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:33,876
I have no one on my side.

193
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:38,881
I can't even trust
the people I used to trust.

194
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:44,428
But none of this is my fault.
I know it isn't.

195
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:58,400
[nurse] Ms. Kang Jisun,
your medication is ready.

196
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,862
Oh, sorry. I forgot.

197
00:22:09,495 --> 00:22:10,496
Here you go.

198
00:22:19,213 --> 00:22:24,718
FOR WHEN I AM WEAK, THEN I AM STRONG

199
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:50,578
[Junho] <i>Mother, I'm here.</i>

200
00:22:50,661 --> 00:22:51,996
[caregiver] Oh, good to see you.

201
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,247
[Junho chuckles] Hello.

202
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:56,667
The physical therapist is here,
helping her with her exercises.

203
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,961
She's been waiting for you
for quite a while.

204
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:00,504
Come on in.

205
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:03,757
[physical therapist] Just put it down.

206
00:23:03,841 --> 00:23:05,092
That's it.

207
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:08,220
Now your left foot, just a little.
Well done.

208
00:23:08,304 --> 00:23:10,139
Okay, one more time.

209
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:11,807
Left foot…

210
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:14,351
Put your weight on it, and…

211
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:16,729
left foot.

212
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:17,897
Well done.

213
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:21,442
Are you feeling a little better?

214
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:25,321
Seeing you must've given her a boost.

215
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,489
She's moving much more smoothly
all of a sudden.

216
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:29,825
Please help her make up

217
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:32,077
-for all the sessions she's missed.
-[physical therapist] Okay.

218
00:23:32,161 --> 00:23:34,288
[Junho's mom slurring] Go upstairs.

219
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:36,498
[caregiver] She wants you to go upstairs.

220
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:39,960
I think she doesn't want you
to see her struggling.

221
00:23:40,044 --> 00:23:42,046
Okay, I'll be upstairs.

222
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:44,131
But you have to finish your session today.

223
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:45,633
-Okay.
-All right.

224
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:52,681
Let's start with your right foot again.

225
00:26:48,857 --> 00:26:52,027
These are your favorite flowers.

226
00:26:56,824 --> 00:26:57,825
Marguerites.

227
00:27:00,327 --> 00:27:01,411
They mean…

228
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:06,083
"true love."

229
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:15,717
My daughter saw Junho
giving our cat some treats.

230
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:20,264
Where did you take our cat?

231
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,099
What did you do to it?

232
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:29,523
Junho, tell me.

233
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,067
Did you hide the cat?

234
00:27:33,402 --> 00:27:34,862
I haven't seen it.

235
00:27:41,994 --> 00:27:42,995
[Mother] Junho.

236
00:27:43,704 --> 00:27:44,705
Gosh.

237
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,499
Junho…

238
00:28:12,441 --> 00:28:13,734
Do you remember?

239
00:28:15,569 --> 00:28:18,071
The first time you caught me lying.

240
00:28:21,617 --> 00:28:23,619
You were so angry with me.

241
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:27,080
-[water running]
-[Mother] Lying is filthy.

242
00:28:27,623 --> 00:28:29,333
[Junho] <i>You scrubbed my mouth so hard…</i>

243
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:32,377
[Mother] You have to wash
that filthy mouth clean.

244
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:35,756
<i>…with soapy water.</i>

245
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,557
I love you,

246
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:11,268
Mother.

247
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:57,689
Huh?

248
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:01,109
Why me?

249
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:14,164
This guy…

250
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:16,333
[Realtor] <i>You wanted us</i>
<i>to sell the house quickly, right?</i>

251
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:18,335
<i>I was going to show</i>
<i>the buyer around myself,</i>

252
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:21,046
<i>but another client came in</i>
<i>with an urgent deal. </i>[chuckles]

253
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:24,299
<i>It'll be just one guy,</i>
<i>and he can stop by at any time.</i>

254
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:32,182
-Oh, sorry to keep you waiting.
-Oh, no, that's okay.

255
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:34,142
-[Realtor] Shall we go in? Right this way.
-Sure.

256
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:41,441
[Realtor] Ma'am!

257
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:42,859
Are you home?

258
00:31:43,819 --> 00:31:46,613
That's strange. She said she'd be home.

259
00:31:55,831 --> 00:31:56,832
Shoot!

260
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,503
I can hear a phone ringing inside.

261
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:02,921
Could she be asleep?

262
00:32:04,798 --> 00:32:06,550
-[doorbell rings]
-[phone ringing stops]

263
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:10,178
-Ma'am, we're here to see the house!
-[Jisun sighs]

264
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,429
Sparkle Real Estate!

265
00:32:13,682 --> 00:32:14,683
Ma'am?

266
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:17,644
[Jisun] Yes, I know…

267
00:32:20,147 --> 00:32:22,399
[Realtor] Oh, you are home.
Great. [chuckles]

268
00:32:22,482 --> 00:32:24,025
We'll just have a look around then.

269
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:25,652
Come on in. Right this way.

270
00:32:39,875 --> 00:32:44,045
Yes. Wow, this place is perfect
for someone living alone. [laughs]

271
00:32:44,129 --> 00:32:45,839
Come on in and take a look, sir.

272
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:47,048
Please, come in.

273
00:32:47,132 --> 00:32:49,426
[Realtor] Wow, it's southeast-facing!

274
00:32:49,509 --> 00:32:52,637
You'll get plenty of sunlight all day,
starting in the morning!

275
00:32:52,721 --> 00:32:54,848
Now, this way to the master bedroom.

276
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:56,349
Right over there.

277
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:58,268
This is the master bedroom.

278
00:32:58,351 --> 00:32:59,978
Wow, it's spacious!

279
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:02,898
You could put some built-in
wardrobes along this wall.

280
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:06,484
It'd make the room really nice and cozy,
don't you think? [laughs]

281
00:33:07,152 --> 00:33:11,072
Looks like that area's been renovated too.

282
00:33:12,616 --> 00:33:14,159
Oh, wow.

283
00:33:15,285 --> 00:33:17,787
Why don't you take a look
at the bathroom too?

284
00:33:17,871 --> 00:33:18,872
Here.

285
00:33:20,832 --> 00:33:23,210
-[water running]
-The water pressure's great too!

286
00:33:24,586 --> 00:33:27,005
And there's a window,
so you get good ventilation.

287
00:33:27,088 --> 00:33:29,174
-Thank you for showing us around.
-Sure.

288
00:33:30,175 --> 00:33:31,593
-[Realtor] We'll be going now.
-Okay.

289
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:33,470
[Realtor] Oh, and one more thing.

290
00:33:33,553 --> 00:33:35,597
Don't list the house
with any other agents.

291
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:36,681
I'll find you a buyer.

292
00:33:36,765 --> 00:33:39,434
-Okay.
-All right, then. Bye.

293
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:40,685
Let's go.

294
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:01,623
Hello?

295
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:04,334
[Realtor] <i>Ma'am, check your bank account.</i>

296
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:06,670
<i>The man who viewed your house earlier,</i>
<i>Kim Namu,</i>

297
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:08,838
<i>says he's transferred</i>
<i>the deposit to hold it.</i>

298
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:12,092
Already?

299
00:34:12,175 --> 00:34:14,261
<i>He says you can choose the moving date.</i>

300
00:34:14,344 --> 00:34:17,180
<i>He's living in company housing,</i>
<i>so he's flexible.</i>

301
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:20,392
<i>He must've</i>
<i>really liked the place. </i>[laughs]

302
00:34:24,562 --> 00:34:26,106
-[paper shuffling]
-[Realtor] Take your time

303
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:27,232
and read through it. [chuckles]

304
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:28,316
Okay.

305
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:30,360
[Realtor] Since you haven't found
a new place yet,

306
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:32,487
I've set the moving date
well into the future.

307
00:34:32,570 --> 00:34:34,864
We can discuss it
and finalize the date before then.

308
00:34:35,573 --> 00:34:36,574
Does that sound okay?

309
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:40,453
Now, sign here, please.

310
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:41,788
-Yes.
-Here.

311
00:34:56,052 --> 00:34:57,053
[Namu] Wait.

312
00:35:00,557 --> 00:35:04,227
Do you happen to know
any good places to eat around here?

313
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:07,188
Places to eat?

314
00:35:07,689 --> 00:35:09,983
Yeah, I thought I'd ask while I'm here.

315
00:35:10,609 --> 00:35:11,985
And it's lunchtime anyway.

316
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:15,947
What kind of food?

317
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:19,367
Anything's fine.

318
00:35:19,451 --> 00:35:21,036
I'm not a picky eater.

319
00:35:23,038 --> 00:35:24,581
Well, there's…

320
00:35:26,082 --> 00:35:28,501
There's a place across the street
that serves <i>ssambap</i>.

321
00:35:28,585 --> 00:35:31,296
Oh. Do they serve single portions?

322
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,715
They might not.

323
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,884
-Let me think of somewhere else--
-Actually…

324
00:35:38,011 --> 00:35:40,847
Would you like to have lunch together,
if you don't mind?

325
00:35:48,521 --> 00:35:52,400
After we eat, you can just go on your way.

326
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:59,616
You gave me a good deal on the house,
so I just wanted to thank you.

327
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:03,912
But if you'd rather not, just say so.

328
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:17,842
I've been meaning to come here,
but never got around to it.

329
00:36:19,386 --> 00:36:22,806
Whenever I pass by,
there's always a long line outside.

330
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:27,977
-Here you go.
-[Jisun] Thank you.

331
00:36:31,773 --> 00:36:32,774
Come to think of it,

332
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:35,694
there are quite a few places
around here I still haven't tried.

333
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:48,623
[Namu] Thank you.

334
00:36:49,999 --> 00:36:51,418
-[server] Enjoy your meal.
-Thank you.

335
00:36:54,087 --> 00:36:55,714
This place really is amazing.

336
00:36:57,674 --> 00:36:59,509
-Let's dig in.
-[Namu] Let's.

337
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:08,184
You saw the articles?

338
00:37:10,854 --> 00:37:13,440
Then you must know about what happened…

339
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:17,569
[Namu] I did read them
but I didn't believe them.

340
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:21,197
[groans] The reporting was terrible.

341
00:37:22,449 --> 00:37:24,951
They were trying
to completely ruin my reputation.

342
00:37:25,618 --> 00:37:27,078
I even lost my job because of it.

343
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:31,958
Hold on.

344
00:37:34,085 --> 00:37:36,296
Then did you already know
about my house when you…

345
00:37:36,379 --> 00:37:37,714
Oh, no.

346
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:39,215
Please don't get the wrong idea.

347
00:37:42,719 --> 00:37:43,970
NOLBU REAL ESTATE

348
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:45,388
[Namu] Yes, hello?

349
00:37:45,472 --> 00:37:47,182
[Realtor] <i>Hello,</i>
<i>this is Nolbu Real Estate.</i>

350
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:49,058
<i>You haven't found a house yet, have you?</i>

351
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:50,810
I actually have.

352
00:37:51,561 --> 00:37:53,313
I found a place that matched my budget.

353
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:56,149
[exclaims] <i>Really?</i>

354
00:37:56,232 --> 00:37:58,443
<i>Is it that detached house</i>
<i>listed for a quick sale?</i>

355
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:00,820
<i>-The one where a woman lives alone?</i>
-Yes.

356
00:38:00,904 --> 00:38:03,782
<i>That house isn't a good choice.</i>

357
00:38:03,865 --> 00:38:06,451
<i>It's best to avoid places</i>
<i>where something bad has happened.</i>

358
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:08,077
What happened there?

359
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:12,999
<i>Well, it's a little awkward to bring up,</i>
<i>but you should know.</i>

360
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:17,962
<i>The woman living there was in the news</i>
<i>for being sexually assaulted.</i>

361
00:38:18,046 --> 00:38:19,130
Sexual assault?

362
00:38:19,631 --> 00:38:22,175
<i>But some say</i>
<i>she was after the man's money.</i>

363
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:25,053
<i>Anyway, it sounds like</i>
<i>she's got some issues.</i>

364
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:27,847
<i>I know you're a man,</i>
<i>but you'll be living alone too.</i>

365
00:38:27,931 --> 00:38:30,266
<i>I'd stay away from a place</i>
<i>with that kind of history.</i>

366
00:38:31,434 --> 00:38:32,769
I don't care about that.

367
00:38:32,852 --> 00:38:34,521
I've already agreed to buy it.

368
00:38:34,604 --> 00:38:35,855
<i>I see.</i>

369
00:38:35,939 --> 00:38:37,357
<i>All right then.</i>

370
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:39,692
All right, thank you.

371
00:38:45,657 --> 00:38:47,283
<i>Hey, wait.</i>

372
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:49,786
-Wait--
-Don't touch me!

373
00:38:53,623 --> 00:38:55,708
Have you ever been through
something like this?

374
00:38:58,336 --> 00:39:04,884
Something happens, and overnight,
it's like your whole world has changed.

375
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:06,970
Why me?

376
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:16,437
[Namu] <i>Actually…</i>

377
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:20,108
<i>ever since we parted ways that day</i>…

378
00:39:22,235 --> 00:39:24,028
<i>I've thought about you from time to time.</i>

379
00:39:25,613 --> 00:39:27,323
<i>I've been curious about you.</i>

380
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:33,204
I even wished I'd asked for your number.

381
00:39:35,957 --> 00:39:38,543
But the house?

382
00:39:38,626 --> 00:39:41,504
I swear to God,
that was a complete coincidence.

383
00:39:42,005 --> 00:39:43,923
I feel like I'm being
unfairly accused here.

384
00:39:44,007 --> 00:39:45,925
This just doesn't feel right.

385
00:39:53,349 --> 00:39:54,350
[Namu] Sorry?

386
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:58,563
[Jisun] After everything
I've been through to get here…

387
00:40:03,318 --> 00:40:05,403
I love my home
and this neighborhood so much.

388
00:40:10,533 --> 00:40:12,994
And there are still
so many restaurants I haven't tried.

389
00:40:15,288 --> 00:40:17,248
I'll never get to see this ocean again.

390
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,628
Why should I be the one
who has to run away again?

391
00:40:27,133 --> 00:40:28,927
You're right. That's not fair at all.

392
00:40:32,972 --> 00:40:34,182
I'm not moving.

393
00:40:36,559 --> 00:40:39,062
Sorry, but I can't just leave like this.
It's too unfair.

394
00:40:59,415 --> 00:41:02,710
I'm really sorry
for causing you so much trouble.

395
00:41:05,171 --> 00:41:06,255
It's okay.

396
00:41:07,548 --> 00:41:09,175
We all have moments like that.

397
00:41:13,179 --> 00:41:14,639
When we cause trouble for others?

398
00:41:16,933 --> 00:41:18,101
No.

399
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:23,606
Moments when it feels like
life is being cruel only to you.

400
00:41:30,530 --> 00:41:32,198
You know, Mr. Kim Namu,

401
00:41:33,658 --> 00:41:35,493
I think you're a really good person.

402
00:41:41,082 --> 00:41:42,667
I'm glad.

403
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:44,002
About what?

404
00:41:45,086 --> 00:41:46,713
You said you love it here,

405
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:49,173
especially the ocean.

406
00:41:52,635 --> 00:41:54,137
I was hoping…

407
00:41:55,930 --> 00:41:58,683
you wouldn't leave, Jisun.

408
00:42:11,154 --> 00:42:15,324
Well, I hope you find an even better house
and that everything works out for you.

409
00:42:20,788 --> 00:42:22,040
Will you be okay?

410
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:25,752
What do you mean?

411
00:42:29,839 --> 00:42:30,840
Just…

412
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:32,925
everything…

413
00:42:39,432 --> 00:42:41,267
Not everything is okay.

414
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:45,897
But things will get better.

415
00:42:52,111 --> 00:42:53,279
Jisun.

416
00:42:55,364 --> 00:42:58,951
There's nothing wrong with you.

417
00:43:03,331 --> 00:43:04,332
Sorry?

418
00:43:06,334 --> 00:43:07,877
You're not strange

419
00:43:08,836 --> 00:43:10,588
and you're not overly sensitive.

420
00:43:13,883 --> 00:43:18,054
You're doing really well, Jisun.

421
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:29,774
Thank you.

422
00:43:59,846 --> 00:44:01,806
What's with that guy?

423
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:15,903
-INTERESTED
-CAN WE MEET IN PERSON?

424
00:44:15,987 --> 00:44:19,574
DELETED ACCOUNT
LAST ACTIVE A LONG TIME AGO

425
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:56,402
SEARCH
HIGH-PAYING GIGS FOR MINORS

426
00:45:03,743 --> 00:45:05,453
<i>I put in a good word for you.</i>

427
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:08,956
<i>Turns out a former classmate of mine</i>
<i>knows the director of that clinic.</i>

428
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:10,708
Thank you.

429
00:45:11,417 --> 00:45:13,294
I owe you a drink
somewhere nice next time.

430
00:45:31,354 --> 00:45:36,025
The director at White
told me you're a doctor.

431
00:45:36,943 --> 00:45:38,694
It's nice to meet you at last.

432
00:45:38,778 --> 00:45:41,948
I wonder when we medical professionals
will finally be safe from patients

433
00:45:42,031 --> 00:45:43,616
who might try to kill us.

434
00:45:46,285 --> 00:45:48,704
Here's the medical report on Kang Jisun.

435
00:45:48,788 --> 00:45:50,081
Thank you.

436
00:45:51,916 --> 00:45:55,127
"Elevated levels of depression and anger,

437
00:45:55,211 --> 00:45:58,965
with a risk of self-harm
or other dangerous behavior."

438
00:46:02,885 --> 00:46:07,223
If she's shown signs of illegal
or violent behavior driven by delusions…

439
00:46:09,392 --> 00:46:11,936
it would be safer
to have her committed, right?

440
00:46:13,229 --> 00:46:14,230
Committed?

441
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:17,191
You mean hospitalizing her
against her will?

442
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:24,949
Excuse me. I'm with the police.

443
00:46:25,825 --> 00:46:26,993
[owner] Okay.

444
00:46:28,869 --> 00:46:29,870
Number 50.

445
00:46:29,954 --> 00:46:32,039
Just head straight down that way.

446
00:46:39,922 --> 00:46:41,549
"Romantic Monster"?

447
00:46:46,387 --> 00:46:50,433
You know GHB is a narcotic, right?

448
00:46:54,145 --> 00:46:55,980
The person selling it

449
00:46:57,940 --> 00:47:00,776
posted an online ad
offering high pay for delivery jobs.

450
00:47:00,860 --> 00:47:03,696
SIMPLE DELIVERY ERRANDS
MINORS WELCOME, NO FACE-TO-FACE CONTACT

451
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:05,281
"Romantic Monster."

452
00:47:07,033 --> 00:47:09,910
We found messages
exchanged using your account.

453
00:47:12,455 --> 00:47:15,624
Did you deliver it
without knowing what it was?

454
00:47:22,423 --> 00:47:23,924
Did someone tell you to do it?

455
00:47:29,305 --> 00:47:30,306
Min Junho.

456
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:33,642
We called your father.

457
00:47:34,852 --> 00:47:37,480
You don't have to talk right now
if you don't want to. But…

458
00:47:44,737 --> 00:47:46,447
[Junho] Hyunsoo, what's going on?

459
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:54,538
-Get up.
-I'm still questioning him.

460
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:03,047
As you know, drug couriers…

461
00:48:05,049 --> 00:48:06,592
We call them runners.

462
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:11,430
Even though he's underage
and claims he didn't know what it was,

463
00:48:12,890 --> 00:48:16,102
he could still be sent
to a juvenile detention center.

464
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:19,730
Do you have any evidence?

465
00:48:19,814 --> 00:48:21,148
We're still investigating.

466
00:48:27,405 --> 00:48:28,406
By any chance…

467
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:36,080
Do you know who may have ordered
your son to transport GHB, Mr. Min?

468
00:48:49,593 --> 00:48:53,097
When are you due?

469
00:48:57,184 --> 00:48:58,811
As you know…

470
00:49:00,980 --> 00:49:04,316
there are things we'd never want
our children to see.

471
00:49:06,026 --> 00:49:08,696
Things you'd never want them to know.

472
00:49:10,573 --> 00:49:14,285
I hope you have a healthy delivery.

473
00:49:15,035 --> 00:49:16,078
Everyone…

474
00:49:18,998 --> 00:49:22,126
pays the price for what they've done.

475
00:49:46,484 --> 00:49:50,029
[Jisun] <i>"He who fights with monsters</i>
<i>should look to it</i>

476
00:49:50,821 --> 00:49:53,407
<i>that he himself</i>
<i>does not become a monster."</i>

477
00:49:55,868 --> 00:49:58,412
<i>"For when we gaze</i>
<i>into the abyss of a monster,</i>

478
00:50:00,247 --> 00:50:01,457
<i>the abyss also</i>…

479
00:50:04,543 --> 00:50:06,670
<i>gazes back into us."</i>

480
00:50:24,647 --> 00:50:26,065
[Junho] Nice place for a cup of tea.

481
00:50:33,072 --> 00:50:35,115
I'm reporting you
for trespassing and stalking.

482
00:50:36,033 --> 00:50:37,284
[Junho] Got any proof?

483
00:50:38,702 --> 00:50:39,870
Because I do.

484
00:51:03,060 --> 00:51:06,230
You're threatening me with that now?

485
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:10,568
Let's forgo the dirt
we have on each other.

486
00:51:12,403 --> 00:51:13,779
What do you want?

487
00:51:15,281 --> 00:51:16,949
Hyunsoo's been falsely accused.

488
00:51:18,826 --> 00:51:20,619
I think the friend he's trying to protect

489
00:51:20,703 --> 00:51:23,956
<i>is the same girl I lied for</i>
<i>at the hospital before.</i>

490
00:51:25,374 --> 00:51:26,458
<i>Kim Soyeon.</i>

491
00:51:30,546 --> 00:51:34,508
She's the one who used his account
to sell knockoff sneakers before.

492
00:51:35,801 --> 00:51:38,804
I want you to talk to her.

493
00:51:40,347 --> 00:51:42,600
Tell her that
if she doesn't turn herself in,

494
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:43,892
things will only get worse.

495
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:48,772
He's your son.
Why don't you do it yourself?

496
00:51:49,565 --> 00:51:50,899
[Junho] I can't get a hold of her.

497
00:51:52,443 --> 00:51:55,654
I think she has the wrong idea
that I'm pressuring her to protect my son.

498
00:52:00,284 --> 00:52:01,660
And besides…

499
00:52:03,829 --> 00:52:06,915
I figured you'd be better at
encouraging her to tell the truth than me,

500
00:52:08,292 --> 00:52:12,880
being her teacher and all, Ms. Kang Jisun.

501
00:52:15,799 --> 00:52:18,469
I'm giving you a chance.

502
00:52:19,511 --> 00:52:23,182
If you pull this off,
I'm willing to drop the lawsuit.

503
00:52:41,533 --> 00:52:45,746
[Hwayoung] We still haven't identified
the seller or the buyer.

504
00:52:47,915 --> 00:52:52,252
That kid hasn't said a single word
since he got here.

505
00:52:59,635 --> 00:53:01,345
Let me try talking to him.

506
00:53:26,412 --> 00:53:28,622
Last time we were here,

507
00:53:29,707 --> 00:53:34,044
you wanted us to be friends, remember?

508
00:53:48,851 --> 00:53:51,311
They say you have to come back
for questioning tomorrow.

509
00:53:52,563 --> 00:53:56,066
And it might keep going
until you tell them something.

510
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:07,578
[Hyunsoo] You really didn't do it?

511
00:54:11,540 --> 00:54:12,750
Lie, I mean.

512
00:54:20,299 --> 00:54:24,428
Answer me first, and then I'll tell you.

513
00:54:28,348 --> 00:54:29,516
That delivery job…

514
00:54:32,603 --> 00:54:33,896
It wasn't you, was it?

515
00:54:41,069 --> 00:54:42,070
Could it be…

516
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:50,537
Soyeon.

517
00:54:57,211 --> 00:54:58,337
[Soyeon] It wasn't him.

518
00:55:02,090 --> 00:55:03,217
It was me.

519
00:55:08,138 --> 00:55:11,850
Min Hyunsoo didn't know anything about it.

520
00:55:15,437 --> 00:55:17,564
It was all me. I did it using his account.

521
00:55:19,274 --> 00:55:21,777
He got caught
selling knockoff sneakers too.

522
00:55:21,860 --> 00:55:23,445
That was also me.

523
00:55:24,112 --> 00:55:25,906
And you took that delivery job too?

524
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:38,043
I know where the people
running that operation are based.

525
00:55:42,464 --> 00:55:46,093
<i>I left my phone where I made the delivery,</i>
<i>so I went back for it.</i>

526
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:49,930
<i>I saw those people drive off,</i>

527
00:55:50,013 --> 00:55:52,057
<i>and then I saw the same car</i>
<i>outside my academy.</i>

528
00:55:52,140 --> 00:55:53,141
[team leader] Kim Jinuk.

529
00:55:53,725 --> 00:55:57,563
[Soyeon] <i>But then,</i>
<i>I ran into the same people again.</i>

530
00:55:59,940 --> 00:56:01,733
[Jinuk sighs] Damn it.

531
00:56:11,618 --> 00:56:13,787
[Junho] This is the last round, right?

532
00:56:23,297 --> 00:56:25,716
Did Ms. Kang get fired from school
because of you, Dad?

533
00:56:29,344 --> 00:56:30,846
It wasn't because of me.

534
00:56:31,680 --> 00:56:33,140
Why?

535
00:56:33,223 --> 00:56:35,601
I was just wondering
if she could come back to school.

536
00:56:38,270 --> 00:56:39,646
That's not going to happen.

537
00:56:39,730 --> 00:56:42,774
In a just society, people who do wrong
have to face the consequences.

538
00:56:43,817 --> 00:56:45,569
And I'm really angry with you this time.

539
00:56:46,445 --> 00:56:48,655
You know Soyeon isn't
a good friend for you.

540
00:56:50,866 --> 00:56:53,493
Don't be reckless
and take the blame for someone else again.

541
00:56:57,331 --> 00:56:59,124
Dad, did you really love Mom?

542
00:57:05,881 --> 00:57:07,299
What?

543
00:57:09,760 --> 00:57:11,470
If you did, then you should understand.

544
00:57:12,638 --> 00:57:15,307
Sometimes, you just want to
do that for someone.

545
00:57:27,527 --> 00:57:28,654
The buyer list.

546
00:57:28,737 --> 00:57:29,988
There isn't one.

547
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:32,949
You sell drugs
and don't keep track of your customers?

548
00:57:33,533 --> 00:57:35,994
If you go to prison this time,
you're not getting out.

549
00:57:36,078 --> 00:57:38,538
I told you, I don't have one.
What do you want me to do?

550
00:57:45,962 --> 00:57:47,339
-[pedal clangs]
-[water running]

551
00:57:52,552 --> 00:57:53,720
[Junho] It's not easy, is it?

552
00:57:55,097 --> 00:57:57,474
-[Jieun] The patient held up well.
-[pedal clangs]

553
00:57:57,557 --> 00:57:59,393
Not the surgery. I meant life in general.

554
00:57:59,893 --> 00:58:01,103
Family…

555
00:58:02,521 --> 00:58:03,647
and personal matters too.

556
00:58:11,697 --> 00:58:12,823
Dr. Kang Jieun.

557
00:58:16,410 --> 00:58:17,577
We need to talk.

558
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:20,664
I don't want to interfere
in your family affairs,

559
00:58:20,747 --> 00:58:22,749
but there's something we need to discuss.

560
00:58:28,171 --> 00:58:31,925
KANG JISUN
DELUSIONAL DISORDER

561
00:58:32,008 --> 00:58:34,344
She falsely accused me
and broke into my home.

562
00:58:35,679 --> 00:58:39,099
And she even drugged,
abducted, and held me captive.

563
00:58:44,020 --> 00:58:46,815
Ms. Kang Jisun is in
a dangerous situation right now.

564
00:58:47,733 --> 00:58:49,401
<i>There's no point resisting anyway, so…</i>

565
00:58:52,362 --> 00:58:56,116
<i>Stop struggling and just accept it.</i>

566
00:58:59,494 --> 00:59:01,371
CONSENT TO HOSPITALIZATION

567
00:59:01,455 --> 00:59:03,373
Rather than having her
sentenced to prison,

568
00:59:04,166 --> 00:59:05,667
she needs treatment.

569
00:59:05,751 --> 00:59:07,836
It's the only way to protect your sister.

570
00:59:10,756 --> 00:59:11,757
Are you saying…

571
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:16,052
you want me to have
my own sister committed?

572
00:59:20,140 --> 00:59:21,308
I can't.

573
00:59:21,808 --> 00:59:22,809
I won't.

574
00:59:32,319 --> 00:59:34,529
Even if your relationship
with Mr. Park Junghyeon…

575
00:59:37,866 --> 00:59:39,034
comes to light?

576
00:59:41,369 --> 00:59:43,455
INCOMING CALL
JIEUN

577
00:59:51,087 --> 00:59:53,507
MALIGNANT NARCISSISTS AND THEIR VICTIMS

578
00:59:53,590 --> 00:59:54,883
WHO IS THE REAL CULPRIT?

579
01:00:03,350 --> 01:00:07,604
<i>Jisun, Dr. Min Junho came to see me</i>
<i>to threaten me.</i>

580
01:00:07,687 --> 01:00:10,690
<i>He has footage of you putting him</i>
<i>in the car and driving away,</i>

581
01:00:10,774 --> 01:00:12,901
<i>and the footage of you entering his house.</i>

582
01:00:12,984 --> 01:00:14,361
<i>Is any of this true?</i>

583
01:00:18,365 --> 01:00:19,491
[officer] Ma'am.

584
01:00:29,334 --> 01:00:30,418
Sir.

585
01:00:31,962 --> 01:00:32,963
Let's go.

586
01:01:03,159 --> 01:01:04,327
Min Junho!

587
01:01:24,139 --> 01:01:25,390
[Hwayoung] Min Junho,

588
01:01:26,224 --> 01:01:28,935
you're under arrest
for violating the Narcotics Control Act.

589
01:01:33,398 --> 01:01:35,692
Well, I've still got one ace up my sleeve.

590
01:01:38,361 --> 01:01:39,487
Tell me everything.

591
01:01:40,196 --> 01:01:42,574
If it's not the guy I'm looking for,
the deal's off.

592
01:01:42,657 --> 01:01:43,658
[officer] Ma'am.

593
01:02:33,708 --> 01:02:37,629
THE PERFECT LIE

594
01:03:02,696 --> 01:03:03,738
[Hwayoung] <i>He'll be prosecuted.</i>

595
01:03:05,740 --> 01:03:07,951
I think he recorded what he did to me.

596
01:03:08,743 --> 01:03:12,205
<i>We'll have to find another way now.</i>

597
01:03:12,288 --> 01:03:15,250
[person] <i>It looks like you're heading out</i>
<i>to sea to dump a body or something.</i>

598
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:16,793
Can I really trust you?

599
01:03:20,296 --> 01:03:22,882
<i>We have to stop anyone else</i>
<i>from becoming a victim.</i>

600
01:03:22,966 --> 01:03:24,968
[Junho] <i>Don't let that woman leave.</i>

601
01:03:26,511 --> 01:03:30,390
-[siren blaring]
<i>-</i>[Jisun] <i>So it's really over now.</i>

602
01:03:47,032 --> 01:03:48,658
THE PERFECT LIE

603
01:03:48,742 --> 01:03:50,744
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
